course: dictionary
lesson: 1386
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The clues in the sentence show you which meaning the writer means. «Maddie became captain of the girls' football team.» Football and team are the clues, so captain means the leader of a sports team.
explain: «The captain steered the ship through the storm.» Ship and steered are the clues now, so captain means the person in charge of a ship. It is the same word with a different meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to choose.
explain: Captain can also be a verb, a doing word. «Maddie captained the team all season» means she led the team. To check, put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: A captain can be the person in charge of a ship or an aeroplane.
fact: A captain can be the leader of a sports team, like the team captain who talks to the referee.
fact: A captain can be an officer in the army, navy or police.
fact: As a verb, «captain» means to lead a team or a ship.
fact: «Captain James Cook» mapped the coasts of New Zealand and eastern Australia around 1770.
exercise: «The captain of the ship checked the map.» What does captain mean here? | To lead a team | The leader of a sports team | An officer in the police | *The person in charge of a ship
exercise: «Maddie was made captain of the girls' football team.» What does captain mean here? | *The leader of a sports team | A soldier in the army | A sailor who cooks on a boat | The person in charge of an aeroplane
exercise: «Maddie captained the team all season.» What does captained mean? | Lost every match | *Led the team | Sat on the bench | Scored the most goals
test: «Captain James Cook mapped the coasts of New Zealand.» What kind of captain was he? | A pilot who flew over the sea | An army officer in a city | A football team leader | *A ship's captain who sailed and mapped coasts
test: «A bossy captain isn't a good one.» What does this suggest about a good captain? | Is always the loudest | Sits out every game | Never leads anyone | *Is not bossy
exam: «Ella looked out of the window and saw the captain of the aeroplane.» What does captain mean in this sentence? | To lead a team | An army officer | *The chief pilot in charge of the aeroplane | Leader of a sports team
